Cole, male gnomish ranger, went to his reward last evening, my 7th
ascension.  kind of a weird game in some ways--probably no weirder
than anything else, but weird in ways I hadn't yet seen.

one of the first things that happened was getting a bones level
containing a previous Cole's wished-for SDSM (fountain wish, IIRC).
next up was a trip to Minetown, where I found a coaligned temple, so I
sacrificed awhile and received Magicbane, which served me well through
the game.

Sokoban, for the first time since I recently resumed playing nethack
after a couple years off, contained the BoH.  one of this game's minor
frustrations was the absolute plethora of such bags after scarcely
being able to find one in previous games.  I think I counted 5 of
them, all but one in the main dungeon or the mines (none from bones).
I also polyed up a couple but didn't keep them, as I wanted them to
turn into magic markers.

the bigroom yielded several giants--saved them for last, then tried to
scatter them so I could kill and eat one at a time and then leave the
level to work off the satiation.

at some point, I ate a tengu corpse, hoping for teleport control, but
I got the other effect instead, which made navigating the quest a bit
interesting.  as for the quest itself, it was quite easy, and Scorpius
went down quickly.  my uncontrolled teleportitis lasted through lots
of tengu camping until I got bored, cleared the castle, and wished for
cursed scrolls of genocide.  I only got one, and all 4 of the corpses
from the resulting 5 tengu I summoned were useless, but I could then
write a second, which finally yielded a helpful corpse.  other uses of
the castle wand mostly included ?oChrg, ?oGD (below), and magic
markers, which I never found elsewhere.

I did a little polypiling at the castle as well, mostly because Izchak
had only 6 candles in stock, the only ones I found until I'd been
through Gehennom a number of times.  also got a magic marker out of my
polypiling, charged to 1:93.

Gehennom was annoying, as I didn't genocide L until just before I
retrieved the amulet.  nothing I couldn't handle most of the time, of
course, almost except for one L who surrounded me with several dragons
on a no-teleport level.  (I know, /oTeleport at monsters.  didn't
think of it at the time.)  I didn't genocide disenchanters until one
of the zoos in Rodney's tower, where there were 4 or 5 who weren't
sleeping--just wasn't in the mood to deal with them individually.

the run back up with the Amulet was a little more difficult than
usual, with Rodney hounding me almost constantly through Gehennom (but
not much in the main dungeon).  just before starting the Planes, as I
was getting the last of my armour up to +5, I lost my +4 GoP.  I
assume my shield had gotten cursed along the way, and I didn't see
that it was still on when I read a scroll to disenchant my GoP.  that
scroll worked on the shield instead (which I also didn't notice), and
then the blessed scroll enchanted and vapourised the gauntlets.
fortunately, I still had +4 GoD and lots of marker charges, and I
managed to straighten out my shield and get the GoD to +5 without
incident.

I had stupidly walked into some water on my way to Rodney's tower and
didn't realise until I was on the Plane of Earth that I'd lost my
uncursed scrolls of gold detection to that incident.  I toughed it
out, using the Longbow's telepathy and my ranger's automatic searching
to find Earth's portal.  burned my one surviving ?oGD (cursed) on Air
and just made a run for it.  only fought two AEs for any length of
time--may not have killed one or both.  Fire was a pain without the
?oGD, but I just swivel-hipped my way through everyone (while
levitating) until I found the portal.  wished my wand to dust to get
another ?oGD on Water--happily, it took only a very few attempts to
get that wish.  I guess I could have written a scroll, but I don't
think I was entirely aware that I still had a marker on me.

I threw on my =confl on the Astral Plane, an idea I had just a day or
two before re-subscribing to RGRN and seeing that trick posted here a
number of times from the past couple months.  heh.  had to hit all
three altars, but it wasn't too difficult overall--the +7 Longbow and
accompanying +7 arrows made short work of the riders, and everyone
else fell to Magicbane or wands of death (or the conflict from my
ring, I suppose).  it also just didn't seem very crowded up there.

speaking of tricks from RGRN, I like the suggestions to levelport to
the sanctum level and quaff a cursed !oGL to get out.  that helped, as
I landed near the sanctum on the way down and outside of the staircase
moat on the way up.

some of the weird stuff I alluded to at the top:
- copious BoH, as I mentioned, but only particularly weird/"funny" in
  the face of previous games' lack thereof
- ZERO altars in the main dungeon--luckily found a +oID eventually so
  I could stop making minetown runs to check BUC status
- only 3 or 4 vaults, but one did contain Ludios, for whatever that
  was worth to me

it took me until I was composing this post to realise why my final AC
was so low--it had been -53 (-52 with the +4 oilskin cloak that I
forgot to replace with my +5 robe after Water) until the *very* end of
the game.  I think I accidentally zapped the High Priest of Venus with
a /oDeath on my way to the altar.  dangit.  (more annoyed about what I
did than its consequences, as when I did it made the AC hit all but
irrelevant.)

